## 3. Datasets Used

### 3.1 Face Liveness / Spoof Detection Dataset
- **Name:** Real and Fake Face Detection
- **Source:** CIPLAB, Yonsei University (Kaggle)
- **Size:** 2,041 images (1,081 real, 960 fake/GAN-manipulated)
- **Purpose:** Training the liveness/anti-spoofing classifier
- **Format:** JPG images, organized in `training_real/` and `training_fake/` folders

### 3.2 Face Verification Dataset (Selfie vs ID)
- **Name:** Selfie & Official ID Photo Dataset (18K images)
- **Source:** AxonData / Axon Labs (Kaggle)
- **Content:** Diverse selfie + ID-style photo pairs across ethnicities (South Asia, Middle East, African, Hispanic, Caucasian) and numbered sample sets (selfies + docs)
- **Purpose:** Testing and validating the face-matching engine (selfie-to-ID verification)
- **Format:** JPEG images, organized by demographic groups and per-person folders

### 3.3 Deepfake Detection Dataset
- **Name:** DFDC (Deepfake Detection Challenge) — Sample Subset
- **Source:** Kaggle Competition (official lightweight sample, ~4GB)
- **Size:** 400 training videos + metadata.json (labels)
- **Class distribution:** 77 REAL, 323 FAKE videos (imbalanced, handled via weighted loss)
- **Purpose:** Training the deepfake/video-manipulation detection model
- **Format:** MP4 videos with REAL/FAKE labels

### 3.4 Document/OCR Testing Data
- **Approach:** Synthetic mock ID cards generated programmatically (PIL), plus real-world document images used for live API testing (e.g., a physical ID photograph)
- **Fields simulated:** Name, Father Name, Date of Birth, ID Number, Gender, Expiry Date, MRZ zone (TD3 format)
- **Purpose:** Validating the OCR/document field-extraction pipeline
- **Note:** MRZ (Machine Readable Zone) parsing was evaluated using passporteye but requires high-resolution scans with OCR-B monospace fonts for reliable detection — documented as a supported architecture capability, not live-demoed due to resolution constraints
- **Known limitation:** Field-to-label mapping uses a Y-coordinate positional heuristic, which can misassign fields on non-standard document layouts — a documented area for future improvement

## 4. Modules Built

### 4.1 Document Intelligence (OCR) Module
- **Technology:** EasyOCR (pretrained, no custom training required)
- **Functionality:**
  - Extracts text from ID document images
  - Maps detected text to structured fields (Name, DOB, ID Number, etc.) using spatial (Y-coordinate) layout analysis
  - Confidence-based validation with low-confidence warnings
  - Outputs structured JSON
- **Result:** Successfully extracts fields on clear text; correctly flags low-confidence extractions. Field-mapping accuracy varies with document layout — a known limitation for future refinement.

### 4.2 Face-Match Engine
- **Technology:** facenet-pytorch (MTCNN for face detection, InceptionResnetV1 pretrained on VGGFace2 for embeddings)
- **Functionality:**
  - Detects and aligns faces from selfie and ID document images
  - Generates 512-dimensional face embeddings
  - Computes cosine similarity between embeddings
  - Threshold-based match/no-match decision (default threshold: 0.6)
- **Key engineering fix:** Added EXIF orientation correction (`ImageOps.exif_transpose`) to handle phone-camera rotation metadata that was causing face-detection failures

### 4.3 Face Liveness / Spoof Detection Module
- **Technology:** ResNet18 (transfer learning, fine-tuned on layer4 + custom classification head)
- **Training approach:**
  - Initial run: frozen backbone, only final layer trained → 63–66% val accuracy
  - Improved run: unfroze layer4, added data augmentation (horizontal flip, rotation), 10 epochs → 70.66% best validation accuracy
- **Result:** Best model checkpoint saved (`liveness_model_best.pth`); verified working via live API testing with high-confidence predictions (e.g., 99.7%+ on real samples)
- **Known limitation:** Overfitting observed on the small dataset (2,041 images); documented as a baseline suitable for demonstration, with production deployment recommended to use larger datasets (e.g., CelebA-Spoof) for improved generalization

### 4.4 Deepfake Detection Module
- **Technology:** ResNet18 (transfer learning, same fine-tuning approach as liveness model), frame-based video analysis
- **Pipeline:**
  1. Extract N evenly-spaced frames per video (OpenCV)
  2. Crop and align faces from each frame (MTCNN)
  3. Classify each face-frame as real/fake (ResNet18)
  4. Aggregate frame-level predictions into a video-level verdict (average probability)
- **Class imbalance handling:** Weighted CrossEntropyLoss (based on inverse class frequency) to address the 1:4 REAL:FAKE ratio in training data
- **Result:** Verified working end-to-end via live API testing (e.g., 99.98% fake-confidence correctly flagged on a known fake sample)

### 4.5 Trust Scoring Engine (with Explainable AI)
- **Approach:** Rule-based weighted aggregation of all module outputs

| Component | Weight |
|---|---|
| Face Liveness | 25% |
| Face-Match | 30% |
| Deepfake Detection | 30% |
| Document OCR Confidence | 15% |

- **Explainability:** Each component returns a human-readable reasoning string alongside its numeric score
- **Risk categorization:**

| Score Range | Category |
|---|---|
| 80–100 | HIGH TRUST |
| 60–79 | MEDIUM TRUST |
| 40–59 | LOW TRUST |
| 0–39 | REJECT |

- **Result:** End-to-end tested pipeline returning a final trust score with full per-module breakdown and reasoning, verified via `/trust-score` API endpoint

### 4.6 Identity Knowledge Graph
- **Technology:** NetworkX (in-memory graph)
- **Functionality:**
  - Tracks relationships between Users, Documents, Devices, and IP Addresses across verification events
  - Detects shared-document fraud patterns (same document used by multiple users)
  - Detects shared-device fraud patterns (multiple identities verified from the same device)
  - Provides per-user network view (all connected entities and their verification history)
  - Provides overall graph statistics (node/edge counts by type)
- **Result:** Verified working via live API testing — successfully detected a simulated shared-document fraud scenario (`"risk": "HIGH — shared document detected"`) when the same document ID was linked to two different user IDs
- **Known limitation:** Currently in-memory (data resets on server restart); a production deployment would persist this to Neo4j or a similar graph database

### 4.7 AI Identity Copilot
- **Technology:** Groq API (Llama 3.3 70B Versatile)
- **Functionality:**
  - Accepts a free-text analyst question plus verification context data (trust score, module breakdown, etc.)
  - Returns a natural-language explanation grounded strictly in the provided data
  - Separate endpoint auto-generates a concise investigation summary (trust assessment, key risk factors, recommended action) without requiring a specific question
- **Result:** Verified working via live API testing — correctly explained a LOW TRUST verification result by referencing the specific weak components (Face Match, Deepfake Check) from the supplied breakdown

