## 5. Key Engineering Challenges & Solutions

| Challenge | Solution |
|---|---|
| Dataset detachment on Kaggle session restart | Re-attach dataset via "Add Input"; verify with `os.walk()` after every restart |
| Internet access disabled by default on Kaggle | Enabled via Settings → Turn on internet (requires session to be stopped first, and phone-verified account) |
| Face detection failing on rotated phone photos | Applied `ImageOps.exif_transpose()` to correct EXIF orientation before face detection |
| Class imbalance in deepfake dataset (1:4 REAL:FAKE) | Weighted CrossEntropyLoss based on inverse class frequency |
| Overfitting on small liveness dataset | Fine-tuned only layer4 + classifier head (not full network); added data augmentation |
| Python 3.14 venv incompatible with pydantic-core | Rebuilt venv using Python 3.12 for stable FastAPI/Pydantic installation |
| Duplicate/stray model files in `frontend/` risking accidental git commit | Removed duplicates; strengthened `.gitignore` with global `*.pth` pattern |
| No suitable OCR training dataset with real text/MRZ found on Kaggle | Generated synthetic mock ID cards programmatically to validate the OCR pipeline, avoiding real PII/privacy concerns |
| torch/numpy version conflicts after installing facenet-pytorch | Verified as non-blocking dependency warnings; did not affect functionality |
| Docker build stalling on large `torch` wheel download | Identified as a slow/unstable internet connection issue during the ~500MB CUDA-enabled torch download; deferred to a stable-connection session, with CPU-only torch identified as a future size/speed optimization |

